{
  "_comment": "What's Your Retired Name? The reader looks up the first letter of their first name (A-Z) and their birth month (January-December) and reads the two together: 'Captain' + 'Hammock Snoozer'. Every one of the 26 x 12 pairings is printed by implication, so the two lists are written to one shape rather than checked one by one: a FIRST name is a friendly, gender-neutral title or a cheerful one-word nickname; a LAST name is exactly two words, a leisure thing and the doer of it ('Porch Rocker', 'Crossword Champ'). Any first name then reads naturally before any last name. Variety is structural: every requested name gets its own brief (a first-name kind and flavour, or a retirement pastime), shuffled by seed, so one reply cannot be twelve kinds of napping. The name budgets arrive on the request (frontend/src/utils/studio/retired-name/content.ts); limits below are the hard bounds. agentHeads are the doer words a last name may end on besides -er/-or/-ist ones; nonAgentHeads are -er words that are things, not doers. blockedTerms keep sensitive topics, age jokes, insults and gendered words off a page whose names land on everyone.",
